Chapter: BvtStaminaDrain
  cites Uoaix chapter CompositePaging
  cites Uoaix chapter BvtCheck

 UOAIX-245, Damian's example: a carry max of 400 and a bar of 100. A bump costs 1 at any load up to 400, then 2, 3, 4, 5
 at 401 to 404; from 405 the whole bar. A clear step is free through 404 and drains the whole bar from 405.
  bvt-stamina-drain : Integer -> [Console] Integer
  bvt-stamina-drain (unused) = act
    a <- bvt-check "a bump costs 1 empty, at 200 and at the carry max of 400 (UOAIX-245)" (cp-bump-cost 0 400 100 == 1 & cp-bump-cost 200 400 100 == 1 & cp-bump-cost 400 400 100 == 1)
    b <- bvt-check "in the grace a bump costs 2, 3, 4, 5 at 401..404, and from 405 drains the whole bar" (cp-bump-cost 401 400 100 == 2 & cp-bump-cost 402 400 100 == 3 & cp-bump-cost 403 400 100 == 4 & cp-bump-cost 404 400 100 == 5 & cp-bump-cost 405 400 100 == 100 & cp-bump-cost 1000 400 100 == 100)
    c <- bvt-check "a clear step is free at 0, 400 and 404 and drains the whole bar at 405; a bump is never free" (cp-overload-cost 0 400 100 == 0 & cp-overload-cost 400 400 100 == 0 & cp-overload-cost 404 400 100 == 0 & cp-overload-cost 405 400 100 == 100 & cp-bump-cost 0 0 100 >= 1)
    a + b + c
  end
